   "summary": "Information Bulletin No. 15 provides an extensive overview of Western musical culture in Japan, from its Meiji-era foundation under Shuji Izawa and Luther Whiting Mason through the establishment of the Tokyo Academy of Music and the Japan Philharmonic Orchestra. It describes the wartime suppression of Allied music by the militarist Japan Musical Culture Association, followed by postwar democratic cultural revival led by SCAP's Civil Information and Education Section (CIE). The report examines the dissemination of American symphonic works by 36 composers, the postwar stagings of operas by the Fujiwara and Nagato Miho companies, ballet productions, the reconstruction of the war-damaged record manufacturing industry, and the booming popularity of American swing and dance halls among Japanese youth.",
